+
+`enqueue(jobs)` accepts jobs with an ID, optional `dependsOn`, and optional `payload`.
+It rejects malformed, duplicate, unknown, cyclic, or otherwise invalid batches
+without changing the existing checkpoint. `run()` returns the final sorted snapshot;
+concurrent calls share one drain. `snapshot()` returns a detached snapshot.
+
+`onStage(stage, id)` is awaited after durable `claimed` and `completed` transitions.
+On restart, jobs persisted as `running` are returned to `pending` and retried with an
+incremented attempt number.
+
+## Self-test
+
+```text
+node --test test.cjs
+```
+
+## Recovery limitation
+
+This is at-least-once recovery. A process crash after `claimed` and before completion
+can repeat the side effect, so `execute` should be idempotent or use its attempt/job
+identity for deduplication. Atomic checkpoint replacement prevents stale temporary
+files from superseding the committed checkpoint.
